how to get comfortable in front of the  camera I got a great question from one  of my new loyal YouTube viewers is  watching all my stuff Kevin who wrote in  to say that he wants to start doing his  own thing in front of the camera and  he's nervous and he doesn't know how I  do it and he speaks to people all day  but he can't imagine doing it in front  of the camera where he's got nobody to  talk to and it's just him in the camera  and how do you get started how do you  get comfortable in front of the camera  so I've got a few tips for you Kevin  that will hopefully help you launch your  YouTube career the first one is practice  it takes a lot of practice when I first  started I sucked on camera I sucked and  I had done TV gigs before I had done a  lot of presentations before but there's  something about being one-on-one in the  camera that I don't know I just sucked  it was terrible it took me it took me  the whole day to do one video and it was  a crappy video but it would just that  took me that long now I sit down and I  can do 10 to 15 videos in one sitting  because of the practice but I've done a  thousand videos literally a thousand  videos is how many I've done that I've  recorded and posted so it's crazy it's  just a lot of work and you get more  comfortable with it just like everything  else you learn something and you're  trying to pick it up it takes you a long  time to get going and then you get  better and better and better and better  and I find when you're creating  something new you may have really good  taste right you may be able to watch  your video and say I love that video you  know Evans video that's great or I love  that Les Brown video or et video or  whatever it is and then you look at what  you make and you realize that it's it's  crap you know it's just it's not good  enough and there's this huge gap between  what you know is good and what you can  create and that's frustrating and that's  where a lot of people will quit but by  pushing through and by making more and  more and getting better you start to get  better where where you know what's good  and you're slowly getting towards that  and your tastes are generally much  higher than everybody else's my first  videos I look at them with horror  I want to take them down look the look  oh my god what that was that was so bad  and anyway I'm my own worst critic right  you're going to be your own worst critic  people still watch those videos they  have thousands of views they still leave  comments and say what a great video  thank you so much and I'm thinking are  you kidding me I was such a bad video  you know the content may have been great  but my delivery and the it's just it was  brutal in my view and now I'm at the  point where I start to enjoy watching my  videos I'm almost almost closed that gap  between what I think is good and what  I'm delivering so I'm getting close it  just takes a ton of work and practice  and you get more comfortable with it  when I very first started doing it I had  to be alone in the room I couldn't have  anybody with me I had to do it by myself  but there's somebody else I'd be worried  that they would be judging me watching  me when I did them with my DSLR camera  it wasn't autofocus so I had to have my  sister or a staff member focus on me and  then out and then press record and have  them leave the room it's ok be by myself  doing it because I get flustered and  nervous with them and I slowly got  better now it doesn't matter people  could be in the room as long as I'm not  making noise I don't care but it just  comes with a lot of practice so you'll  get there but just start and know that  even though your first videos suck and  even though you try to make them as good  as possible they will still suck that's  ok they will get better with time and  with practice don't get down on yourself  and quit the second thing that really  helped me was a caffeine and sugar I  found that when I first started doing  the videos they were pretty boring and  I'd look at them with a wow I'm about to  fall asleep what's happened in this  video and so I started going out and  getting like the venti Frappuccino super  sugar caramel caffeine to the max and I  would I would drink it just before  filming and and in between my videos and  you'll give me more energy so I might  come off as a bit of a spaz on the  camera I stopped having to do that  because I felt you know what I don't I  don't need anymore I'm  I'm I don't know comfortable enough  getting my energy level high to be able  to speak to you guys I'm excited about  what I'm doing but took me a while to  get there same thing for my radio show  and same thing if I was doing some  speaking before I might down this huge  drink or something just to give me some  more energy so to do that that's okay it  gives you your energy it's not super bad  for you  and they'll improve the quality of  product to a point and then the third  thing I found that really helped is I  try to look in the camera and not just  see my reflection of my face there but I  try to look at the person who I'm  talking to  I try to think of somebody who I'm  talking to and visualize that that they  are in front of me so with a youtube  comment like this it's pretty easy so  when you sent in your comment this  little picture of you when I say oh  that's Kevin so I'm talking to Kevin he  looks pretty Chili's got a big smile on  and so I'm I'm thinking of you while I'm  talking to the camera if I'm just trying  to make a point in general about  something that I believe in that's  important frunch Mirza learn about I'll  try to think of somebody who I have in  mind who who I may have told that same  story to when their reaction I try to  visualize them in front of me so I'm not  talking to the camera I'm trying to talk  to a person and I felt that really  helped and then I guess my last tip is  just remember that it doesn't have to be  perfect you know if you make a mistake  this isn't live you can cut it you can  do it again you could try it again and  try it again and try it again so if you  make a mistake it's not the end of the  world but what's important that you get  started and you practice and you get  better and you're passionate about it  and you continue on you do that you'll  eventually be successful and let me know  if you launch your channel you launch  your first video send it to me I'd be  happy to check it out give you some  feedback I'm excited to see it and don't  worry if you think it's crap because  you're on your path and that's important  journey that you've started believe for  those you watching you like the video  please give it a thumbs up below let me  know what you think leave a comment ask  a question I'll give it a response and  if you want to see more videos like this  subscribe to the channel by clicking on  my face  thank you so much and I'll see you soon  you
 

